          I joined National Breathe Free in May 2024, straight out of college.
          As product owner and lead engineer, I designed nearly the entire
          internal platform, with direction from our CTO and development support
          and technical contributions from another engineer.
        </p><p>
          The platform serves 50+ clinics and 300+ total users. Enrichment
          workflows launched in January 2026; the insurance verification
          workflow began development around July and is now live.
        </p><p>
          My hardest engineering decision has been how to scale the ETL pipeline
          efficiently. If I could start again, I would begin with ingestion and
          spend more time on the data model before the frontend.
        </p>
